 78	[here](https://github.com/gfx-rs/wgpu/tree/trunk/examples/features/src/mesh_shader).
 79	
 80	### Features
 81	
 82	- Using mesh shaders requires enabling [`Features::EXPERIMENTAL_MESH_SHADER`].
 83	- Using mesh shaders with multiview requires enabling [`Features::EXPERIMENTAL_MESH_SHADER_MULTIVIEW`].
 84	- Using mesh shaders with point primitives requires enabling [`Features::EXPERIMENTAL_MESH_SHADER_POINTS`].
 85	- Queries are unsupported
 86	- Primitive index support will be added once support lands in for them in general.
 87	
 88	### Backend support and fallback
 89	
 90	Mesh shader support is advertised per adapter through [`crate::Adapter::features`].
 91	The feature is currently exposed by Vulkan, DX12, and Metal, but not by GLES or
 92	WebGPU. Requesting a device with [`Features::EXPERIMENTAL_MESH_SHADER`] when
 93	the adapter does not expose it fails device creation, and
 94	[`Device::create_mesh_pipeline`] requires the feature to be enabled on the
 95	device.
 96	
 97	`wgpu` cannot automatically lower an arbitrary mesh or task shader pipeline to
 98	the vertex pipeline. A task shader controls the mesh dispatch grid and passes a
 99	payload, while a mesh shader produces per-workgroup vertices, primitives, and
100	per-primitive fragment inputs. None of these have a general vertex-shader
101	equivalent. Applications that must run on every adapter should therefore keep
102	a standard render pipeline and select it after querying the adapter:
103	
104	```rust,ignore
105	let mesh_features =
106	    wgpu::Features::EXPERIMENTAL_MESH_SHADER | wgpu::Features::PASSTHROUGH_SHADERS;
107	let mesh_supported = adapter.features().contains(mesh_features);
108	
109	let (device, queue) = adapter
110	    .request_device(&wgpu::DeviceDescriptor {
111	        required_features: if mesh_supported {
112	            mesh_features
113	        } else {
114	            wgpu::Features::empty()
115	        },
116	        required_limits: if mesh_supported {
117	            wgpu::Limits::defaults().using_recommended_minimum_mesh_shader_values()
118	        } else {
119	            wgpu::Limits::downlevel_webgl2_defaults()
120	        },
121	        // SAFETY: enabling experimental features is an explicit opt-in.
122	        experimental_features: unsafe { wgpu::ExperimentalFeatures::enabled() },
123	        ..Default::default()
124	    })
125	    .await?;
126	```
127	
128	The [`mesh_shader` example](https://github.com/gfx-rs/wgpu/tree/trunk/examples/features/src/mesh_shader)
129	follows this pattern to render the same triangle with a mesh pipeline when the
130	feature is available and with a vertex pipeline otherwise.
131	
132	### Limits
133	
134	> **NOTE**: More limits will be added when support is added to `naga`.
135	
136	- `Limits::max_task_mesh_workgroup_total_count` - the maximum total number of workgroups from a `draw_mesh_tasks` command or similar. The dimensions passed must be less than or equal to this limit when multiplied together.

